# Dataset Analysis and Data Types Exploration for Student Performance Data

## Overview
This notebook aims to explore the student performance dataset containing 5000 rows and 15 columns.

## Dataset Columns:
- **StudentID**: Unique identifier for each student
- **Age**: Age of the student
- **Gender**: Gender of the student
- **Ethnicity**: Ethnic background of the student
- **Parental Education**: Level of education attained by the parents
- **Study Time Weekly**: Average hours spent studying per week
- **Absences**: Number of absences
- **Tutoring**: Whether the student receives tutoring or not
- **Parental Support**: Level of parental support
- **Extracurricular**: Participation in extracurricular activities
- **Sports**: Involvement in sports
- **Music**: Participation in music-related activities
- **Volunteering**: Involvement in volunteering activities
- **GPA**: Grade Point Average
- **Grade Class**: Target variable representing the final grade class of the student

## Data Types
- Each column represents various data types (e.g., categorical, numerical). We will analyze and visualize these against the target variable `Grade Class`.